## 5. FEATURE 3 — PERSONALISED LIFESTYLE ADVICE

An extension of the existing plan/interventions model, not a parallel system.

### 5.1 How a recommendation is chosen
Deterministically, by the rules engine, from three inputs already in the
database: questionnaire answers (`questionnaire_responses`), test results
(`test_results`), and — once Wave D lands — genetic results. Each candidate
recommendation carries trigger conditions; the engine evaluates them, ranks by
`impact_weight`, and returns the top N. **No model generates this list.**

### 5.2 What every recommendation must carry
- **Why this matters to you** — the rationale, tied to the specific fact that
  triggered it ("because your fasting insulin was 14 and you told us you sit
  most of the day"), in plain language.
- **What to actually do** — concrete steps with numbers ("a 20-minute walk
  after your largest meal, five days a week"), never "exercise more".
- **How we know** — links to the sources behind it.
- **Make it a habit** — one tap to create a goal (§10) or a reminder (§9).
- **Barriers** — the tips from §11, inline.

### 5.3 Prioritisation
Rank by `impact_weight` (clinician-set, 1–10) × `user_gap` (how far the user
is from target) × `feasibility` (user's own self-reported capacity). Show
**at most three at a time.** A list of fourteen things to change is a list
nobody starts. When one is going well, surface the next.

### 5.4 Data
```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.lifestyle_recommendations (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  slug TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  category TEXT NOT NULL
    CHECK (category IN ('nutrition','movement','sleep','stress','alcohol','smoking','weight','environment')),
  title TEXT NOT NULL,
  plain_summary TEXT NOT NULL,
  rationale TEXT NOT NULL,
  action_steps JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',
  evidence_links JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',
  trigger_conditions JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',  -- read by the rules engine
  impact_weight INT NOT NULL DEFAULT 5,
  contraindications TEXT,
  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'draft'
    CHECK (status IN ('draft','in_review','approved','retired')),
  reviewed_by UUID REFERENCES public.doctors(id),
  reviewed_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.user_recommendations (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  recommendation_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.lifestyle_recommendations(id),
  triggered_by JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',   -- the facts that fired it: shown to the user
  state TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'suggested'
    CHECK (state IN ('suggested','active','paused','done','dismissed')),
  priority_score NUMERIC,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
  UNIQUE (user_id, recommendation_id)
);
```
Clinician review of this table is a queue in `/admin`, reusing the Phase 4
sign-off pattern.

