## 8. FEATURE 6 — REMINDERS AND CHECK-INS

Push, tokens, routing and the in-app inbox already exist (Phase 4). Phase 5
adds *what* we send and the scripted check-in.

### 8.1 Rules
- **Every reminder has a default the user never has to configure**, and every
  default is editable in one screen.
- **Quiet hours are absolute.** Nothing fires 21:00–08:00 local except a
  user-set alarm-style reminder they explicitly placed there.
- **Daily cap.** At most 2 push notifications a day, at most 5 a week, except
  transactional messages (booking confirmed, results ready, order shipped),
  which are uncapped but must still be genuinely transactional.
- **Every push has an in-app twin** in the existing inbox. A user who disabled
  push loses nothing.
- **Dismissal is a signal.** Three ignored reminders of one kind → the app
  asks, once, whether to change the timing or stop them.
- **One-tap snooze and one-tap stop** on every reminder.

### 8.2 The check-in "chatbot" — read this carefully
It is a **scripted, branching, clinician-authored dialogue**. A finite state
machine over a `check_in_scripts` table. It is **not** an LLM, it does not
free-text generate, and it must never appear to give medical advice.

- Questions are closed-form (buttons, scales, yes/no) with an optional free
  text box whose content is **stored and shown to a human, never parsed for
  advice**.
- Any red-flag answer (a symptom from the existing triage list, a suspected
  adverse reaction to a supplement) **exits the script immediately** into the
  existing symptom-triage safe-exit path. This is the single most important
  branch in the feature — test it first.
- Adverse-event answers create a row a clinician sees in the admin queue
  within the working day.
- Check-ins are short: three questions, under thirty seconds.

### 8.3 Data
```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.reminders (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  kind TEXT NOT NULL
    CHECK (kind IN ('habit','supplement','goal','booking_prep','retest','check_in')),
  ref_id UUID,                     -- the goal / recommendation / booking it belongs to
  label TEXT NOT NULL,
  schedule JSONB NOT NULL,         -- {days:[1,2,3], time:"08:30", tz:"Europe/London"}
  active BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,
  snoozed_until TIMESTAMPTZ,
  last_fired_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.check_in_responses (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  script_slug TEXT NOT NULL,
  answers JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',
  flagged BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,   -- red flag → clinician queue
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
