## 10. FEATURE 8 — OVERCOMING BARRIERS

Barriers are content attached to recommendations, surfaced at the moment of
friction rather than filed in a help centre.

- Each `lifestyle_recommendations` row has barrier rows: barrier text,
  strategy, optional resource link, optional recipe/product link.
- Surface them **when the user stalls** — two missed check-ins, a paused goal,
  or an explicit "this is hard" tap that is always visible on a goal card.
- **Normalise first, solve second.** "Most people find the first fortnight
  hardest" before "try this".
- Expert referral (nutritionist, trainer, therapist) is a **vetted directory
  with stated credentials and prices**, and we state plainly whether we take a
  commission.
- **Community and the buddy system (§11) are moderation-gated.** Do not ship
  any user-to-user feature until Section 11.4's requirements are met in full.

```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.barriers (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  recommendation_id UUID REFERENCES public.lifestyle_recommendations(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  category TEXT NOT NULL,          -- 'time','cost','motivation','confidence','access','family'
  barrier_text TEXT NOT NULL,
  strategy_text TEXT NOT NULL,
  resource_url TEXT,
  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'draft',
  reviewed_by UUID REFERENCES public.doctors(id),
  reviewed_at TIMESTAMPTZ
);
```

