## 11. FEATURE 9 — BUDDY SYSTEM  *(Wave D — gated)*

A health app where users discuss cancer risk with strangers is a safeguarding
responsibility, not a social feature.

### 11.4 Ship gates — all required before any user-to-user code goes live
1. A named human moderator with defined hours and an escalation path.
2. Report and block on every surface, reachable in one tap.
3. A written safeguarding policy covering self-harm disclosure, medical
   misinformation between users, and harassment.
4. Automated filtering for crisis language, routing to human review with a
   stated response time and crisis-line signposting.
5. Age verification consistent with the app's terms.
6. **No health data is ever shared automatically.** A buddy sees a display
   name, a chosen goal category, and progress the user explicitly shares.
   Risk scores, results, and genetic data are never buddy-visible — enforce
   in RLS, not in the UI layer.
7. Opt-in, mutual, and leaveable without explanation or friction.

Matching: shared goal category and timezone first; never match on health
status. Provide conversation starters, since most pairs stall at hello.

