## 15. FEATURE 14 — INTERNAL PROGRESS TRACKING

A `/admin` section (Refine, Phase 4 stack), not a new app.

### 15.1 Rules
- **Aggregates only.** The analytics views expose counts and distributions,
  never individual health rows. Identifiable data stays in the clinical
  screens, behind the existing role checks.
- Cohort minimum: **no cell smaller than 10 users** is displayed.
- Build on Postgres views with `security_invoker`, restricted to the
  `analytics` staff role.
- Qualitative feedback is reviewed by a human weekly — free text is where the
  real signal is.
- **Never use the effectiveness data to claim clinical outcomes.** Internal
  learning is not evidence; publishing anything requires a study design.

### 15.2 Measure
Funnel step-through (register → triage → questionnaire → results → **booking**
→ plan → goal set → week 4 retained), drop-off points, goal completion by
category, reminder engagement and opt-outs, adherence vs. measured change,
order and subscription health, support themes.

The **booking step is the number that matters in Wave A**, and week-4 retention
is the number that matters in Wave B.

